sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Payer
    participant App as Payer's app
    participant SB as Sending bank
    participant Sw as Central switch
    participant Dir as Proxy directory
    participant RB as Receiving bank
    participant Payee

    Payer->>App: Enter alias and amount<br/>alias = phone, email, VPA, Pix key
    App->>SB: Payment request

    SB->>Sw: Resolve alias
    Sw->>Dir: Lookup
    Dir-->>Sw: Account, institution, registered name
    Sw-->>SB: Resolved details
    SB-->>App: Show payee name for confirmation<br/>Confirmation of Payee / Verification of Payee
    App-->>Payer: "Pay MARIA S. SANTOS, 250.00?"

    Payer->>App: Authenticate<br/>PIN, biometric, device binding
    App->>SB: Signed authorisation

    Note over SB: The 200ms that decides everything
    SB->>SB: Funds check and hold
    SB->>SB: Sanctions screening
    SB->>SB: Real-time fraud score

    alt Blocked
        SB-->>Payer: Rejected, funds never left
    end

    SB->>Sw: pacs.008 credit transfer<br/>signed, unique end-to-end ID

    Sw->>Sw: Schema and duplicate check
    Sw->>RB: Forward pacs.008

    Note over RB: Receiver has a hard deadline,<br/>typically 4 to 20 seconds
    RB->>RB: Validate account is open,<br/>can receive, not blocked
    RB->>Sw: pacs.002 accept or reject

    alt Accepted
        Sw->>Sw: Move value between settlement accounts<br/>gross now, or net later depending on scheme
        Sw->>SB: pacs.002 confirmation
        Sw->>RB: Settlement confirmed
        RB->>Payee: Funds available, irrevocably
        SB-->>Payer: "Paid" with receipt reference
    else Rejected or timed out
        Sw->>SB: Negative pacs.002 with reason code
        SB->>SB: Release the hold
        SB-->>Payer: Failed, money never left your account
    end

    Note over SB,RB: No chargeback exists.<br/>Recovery requires the receiver's<br/>cooperation or a scheme fraud mechanism.
